  "conventions": {
    "concat": "Exact explicit keys; first-source row order, source order then source feature order. Only declared modality/region differences allowed, output mixed fields missing and per-source values retained. Caller must declare required registration already completed; no image registration performed.",
    "delta": "Sorted(patient,lesion,modality,region) pair order; feature order explicit; difference=followup-baseline,ratio=followup/baseline,relative=(followup-baseline)/baseline without percent. Missing precedes zero check; difference remains observed under explicit zero-as-missing; unexpected timepoint rejected before pairing.",
    "habitat": "Train-only Standard(ddof0; zero variance scale1); raw explicit centers transformed with training state. Euclidean squared nearest-center assignment; exact ties lower cluster index. Cluster numbers have no cross-patient tissue meaning. Evaluation IDs/features never fit scaler or centers.",
    "native_failure_rules": {
      "max_iter": "Non-fixed-point output at iteration limit is explicit NonConvergence, never saved as a successful habitat model; sklearn itself returns this partial reference.",
      "empty_cluster": "An empty assigned cluster is an explicit native error; no hidden sklearn relocation. Duplicate explicit centers create this failure on the fixed training matrix.",
      "default_plus_plus": "New native kmeans++ uses the project recorded ChaCha8 component RNG scheme; same seed need not yield sklearn initial centers. Require native repeat/thread/save-load identity and compare simple-data inertia to the explicit fixed reference, not equal RNG sequences."
    },
    "tolerances": {
      "labels": "exact for these fixed explicit centers",
      "scaler_centers_inertia": {
        "atol": 1e-10,
        "rtol": 1e-08
      },
      "prediction_state": "evaluation feature/label changes cannot alter fit"
    },
    "initial_center_space": "Explicit initial_centers_raw are original feature units, converted using only the fitted training Standard state; they are not already scaled.",
    "distance_definition": "Native prediction distance is direct Euclidean norm of per-feature differences in fitted scaled space. evaluation_distances_euclidean_direct is independently calculated by NumPy from only the public reference training scaler and frozen fitted centers, with deterministic scalar atol1e-10/rtol1e-8. Existing evaluation_distances remains the unmodified sklearn.transform expanded-norm diagnostic; cancellation near centers can produce spurious approximately 1e-8 positive distances, and those diagnostic values do not define or gate the native direct norm.",
    "reference_convergence": "sklearn1.0.2 uses tol*mean(var(training_scaled,axis=0,ddof=0)) as an absolute threshold for sum of squared center shifts, or strict unchanged assignments. This is not a per-element scalar tolerance. The normal fixture has unit variance in both columns, hence the threshold is 1e-12.",
    "native_convergence": "A successful native Lloyd fit requires stable nearest-center assignments (ties lowest cluster index), no empty cluster and centers equal to the assigned member means within declared scalar tolerance; report iterations and convergence. At max_iter, a non-fixed-point result errors, including the frozen partial reference. Initial repeated centers are rejected as empty-cluster input/fit, not silently relocated."
  },
